msgid "The site pings itself whenever a post links internally"
msgstr ""

#: src/Analyze/Rules/SelfPingbackRule.php:114
msgid "Nothing is filtering the ping list, so linking from one post to another on this site makes WordPress send itself a pingback and create a comment."
msgstr ""

#: src/Analyze/Rules/SelfPingbackRule.php:123
msgid "Each internal link costs an HTTP request from the site to itself at publish time and leaves a pingback comment on the linked post that has to be moderated or deleted. Pingbacks to other sites are a different thing and are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: src/Analyze/Rules/SelfPingbackRule.php:132
msgid "Self-pingbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/Analyze/Rules/ShortlinkRule.php:103
msgid "Every page publishes its numeric URL as well as its real one"
msgstr ""

#: src/Analyze/Rules/ShortlinkRule.php:112
msgid "WordPress emits a rel=\"shortlink\" tag in the head and a matching Link: HTTP header, both giving the ?p=<id> form of the page."
msgstr ""

#: src/Analyze/Rules/ShortlinkRule.php:121
msgid "The shortlink is a leftover from an era of character limits. It exposes the internal post id of every page, adds a head tag and an HTTP header to every request, and almost nothing consumes it."
